# MCSP Semantic Definitions — 0.4

**Qualification:** Under Conditional Experiment

This file is the first machine-oriented bridge toward MCSP self-description. It is deliberately independent of ISA mnemonics.

## Definition form

Each semantic construct is represented by:

    DEFINE {
      identity
      category
      inputs
      outputs
      preconditions
      transition
      outcomes
      relations
      realization_constraints
    }

The DEFINE form is itself provisional and must eventually be representable as an MCSP construct.

## Definitions

    DEFINE VALUE {
      category: state-construction
      inputs: value, width
      outputs: destination
      transition: destination receives value under width
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

    DEFINE COPY {
      category: state-transfer
      inputs: source, width
      outputs: destination
      transition: destination receives source value
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

    DEFINE POSITION {
      category: relation
      inputs: base, displacement, index, scale, relation
      outputs: address
      transition: derive address relation
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

    DEFINE READ {
      category: state-transfer
      inputs: address, width, attributes
      outputs: destination
      relations: POSITION, TRANSLATE
      transition: addressed state is observed and transferred to destination
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported | environment-defined
    }

    DEFINE WRITE {
      category: state-transfer
      inputs: address, source, width, attributes
      outputs: addressed-state
      relations: POSITION, TRANSLATE
      transition: source value changes addressed state subject to constraints
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported | environment-defined
    }

    DEFINE COMPUTE {
      category: state-transition
      inputs: operation, values, width, attributes
      outputs: destination
      transition: operation maps input values to output value/state
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

    DEFINE COMPARE {
      category: relation-evaluation
      inputs: relation, values, width
      outputs: condition
      transition: derive condition state
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

    DEFINE BRANCH {
      category: control-transition
      inputs: condition?, target, fallthrough?
      outputs: control-position
      transition: select next control position
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

    DEFINE INVOKE {
      category: control-transition
      inputs: target, continuation, convention
      outputs: control-position, continuation-relation
      transition: transfer control while preserving a continuation relation
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

    DEFINE RETURN {
      category: control-transition
      inputs: continuation, convention
      outputs: control-position
      transition: restore/select continuation control position
      outcomes: completed | exception | unsupported
    }

## Unresolved definitions

The following terms are intentionally not declared closed:

- STATE
- VALUE representation
- width
- relation
- attributes
- TRANSLATE
- condition
- operation
- convention
- exception
- environment-defined
- realization constraint

They form the current self-description residue. The next closure work must decompose them rather than assuming their meaning.
